# La-Z-Boy Playwright Standards

Write reliable, maintainable E2E tests using TypeScript and `@playwright/test`.

---

## 1. Agent Workflow — Discover Before Writing

Before writing any test:
1. Detect the dev server — check `BASE_URL` env var or common ports
2. Navigate and wait for `networkidle` — ensure dynamic content has loaded
3. Inspect the DOM to find real selectors
4. Write the test using what you observed — never guess selectors

```typescript
const BASE_URL = process.env.BASE_URL ?? "http://localhost:3000";
```

Inject identifying headers when running as an agent:
```typescript
await page.setExtraHTTPHeaders({
  "X-Automated-By": "playwright-lazboy",
  "X-Test-Run": process.env.CI ? "ci" : "local",
});
```

---

## 2. Project Structure

```
tests/
├── fixtures.ts                    # Import test/expect from here — NOT from @playwright/test
├── helpers.ts                     # Data generators, API helpers, custom assertions
└── {feature}/
    ├── {feature}-page.ts          # Page Object for this feature
    ├── {feature}.spec.ts          # All tests for this feature
    └── {feature}.md               # Notes on selectors, known edge cases
playwright.config.ts
global-setup.ts
```

---

## 3. Selector Strategy

| Priority | Selector | When |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `getByRole('button', { name: 'Add to Cart' })` | Interactive elements — tests accessibility too |
| 2 | `getByLabel('Email address')` | Form inputs |
| 3 | `getByTestId('product-card')` | Components without stable roles |
| 4 | `getByText('...')` | Static text |
| 5 | CSS selector | Last resort only |

`getByRole` is preferred because it simultaneously tests that the element is accessible to screen readers. If a screen reader can't find it, neither should the test.

### Chaining and filtering

```typescript
// Scope within a parent
const card = page.getByTestId("product-card").filter({ hasText: "Barcelona Recliner" });
const price = card.getByTestId("product-price");

// Filter by child element
const featured = page.getByRole("listitem").filter({
  has: page.getByTestId("featured-badge"),
});

// nth() for indexed items
const first = page.getByTestId("product-card").nth(0);
const last  = page.getByTestId("cart-item").last();
```

### Form inputs

```typescript
await page.getByLabel("Email address").fill("test@lazboy.com");
await page.getByPlaceholder("Search products...").fill("recliner");
await page.getByLabel("Fabric Grade").selectOption("Grade A");
await page.getByRole("checkbox", { name: "Add protection plan" }).check();
```

### Iframes (payment widgets, third-party embeds)

```typescript
const frame = page.frameLocator("#stripe-payment-iframe");
await frame.getByLabel("Card number").fill("4242 4242 4242 4242");
await frame.getByLabel("Expiry date").fill("12/26");
```

### Debugging selectors

```bash
PWDEBUG=1 npx playwright test tests/checkout/checkout.spec.ts
```

