## 4. Writing Tests

```typescript
import { test, expect } from "../fixtures";  // always import from local fixtures

test.describe("Product Detail Page", () => {
  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto("/products/lzb-recliner-001");
    await page.waitForLoadState("networkidle");
  });

  test("adds product to cart",
    { tag: ["@critical", "@pdp", "@PDP-E2E-001"] },
    async ({ page }) => {
      await page.getByRole("button", { name: "Add to Cart" }).click();
      await expect(page.getByTestId("cart-count")).toHaveText("1");
    }
  );
});
```

### Tag every test

| Tag type | Format | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Priority | `@critical`, `@smoke` | Smoke suite for deployments |
| Feature | `@pdp`, `@cart`, `@checkout` | Run one feature: `--grep @checkout` |
| Type | `@e2e`, `@visual`, `@a11y` | Run by test type |
| ID | `@PDP-E2E-001` | Link to ticket/test case |

### Waiting — use expect() auto-retry, not manual waits

```typescript
// Correct — auto-retries until visible or timeout
await expect(page.getByTestId("success-banner")).toBeVisible();

// Wrong — hard-coded waits are fragile and slow
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
```

Use explicit waits only for navigation/network:
```typescript
await page.waitForLoadState("networkidle");  // after navigating to dynamic pages
await page.waitForURL("**/confirmation");     // after form submission
```

